 The effective deployment of heterogeneous detection pipelines depends on using cheap detectors to identify when expensive verification is needed rather than increasing individual detector complexity. Future work will explore temporal modeling for video detection, fine-tuned VLM verifiers for domain-specific forensic cues, and cross-family semantic probe training to remove the per-family retraining requirement.
